+# TPM2-tools Integration Guide (example)
+
+This describes how to use standard tpm2-tools to produce and verify quotes:
+- Device: create EK/AIK, perform quote: tpm2_quote -c <aik.ctx> -l sha256:0,1,2 -m quote.bin -s sig.bin
+- Verifier: use tpm2_checkquote or vendor SDK to check signature with public key and PCRs.
+- Automate: pre-load verifier runs tpm2_quote on device, posts quote and signature to local verifier, which validates and returns OK/FAIL.
+- Best practices: rotate AIK keys via TPM key management, keep EK private in TPM, and log attestation events to MCP for audit.
